What completing quantitative and technical literacy means (@ql-completion: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @quantitative-literacy) { r_2C68EEJZH5KY4Z0DAPKBQEAAZ0
Completion means you can read an unfamiliar technical description, identify its quantities and assumptions, reconstruct and criticize its numerical argument, and produce your own defensible account. Fluent calculation and an independently justified conclusion both matter.

The beginning work includes all three Math for Trades volumes, the needed Prealgebra chapters or the complete book when starting from zero, the specified algebra and trigonometry blocks, Basic Blueprint Reading in full, the SI quantity-and-unit chapters, and the data-organization paper. Complete the exercises and chapter tests appropriate to unfamiliar skills, then demonstrate those skills on different problems. Copying the worked answers is not evidence of this understanding.

The later work includes both complete Mahajan books, the VIM definitions in context, JCGM's uncertainty introduction, and TN 1297 with its assumptions. Complete the technical-claim reading, material-process study, drawing-and-measurement study, infrastructure account, and advanced investigation. Source access and exercise availability vary; the resulting argument and reproducible work matter more than a particular file format.

**Evidence to retain:** a corrected foundation review; a dimensioned drawing and measurement report; a closed and a deliberately nonclosing material account; an annotated real technical claim; a source-backed three-transition infrastructure calculation; and the advanced report with dimensional derivation, uncertainty reasoning, approximation checks, independent-source comparison, and revision. Combine these in one sustained project if it actually demonstrates each kind of reasoning.

Be able to explain an unfamiliar denominator, reject a dimensionally invalid formula, question a dimensionally valid one, distinguish a bound from a standard uncertainty, and identify what observations do not determine. Ask another reader to reproduce a calculation and raise an objection that could change your conclusion. Revise the weak parts instead of treating a checkmark as an answer.

This work supports later mathematics, science, production, logistics, and engineering. It does not establish competence to operate a mine, manufacture a chip, approve a structure, or perform a regulated technical role. Those claims require their detailed subject knowledge, facilities, supervised experience, and appropriate evidence. Keep the shared Records available for reuse whenever a later subject needs their quantities, drawings, or balances.

**Return:** [Quantitative and technical literacy](../Quantitative-literacy.lingua#r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2).
